macOS: use per-thread SC fork admission while retaining the atomic coordinator.

Cider-Topic: sync/msync
Cider-Requires: 0103-msync-lease-admission-and-exit-cleanup.patch
Cider-Status: nondefault performance candidate; complete continuous/performance acceptance pending
Cider-Validation: single-file scoped adversarial review, linked native module, PE32/PE32+ lifecycle

Normal operations publish/recheck their native thread activity instead of
modifying a shared process counter. Fork closes admission and scans registered
threads under the descriptor registry lock, which pins their thread_data. Cold
registration cannot open an inheritable description while that lock is held.
The parent still replaces all descriptor/lease pairs before reopening; the
child still retires the old instance. Shared owner, death proof, commit journal
and notification obligations are unchanged. The cold fork scan is O(threads).

